## 6. Heartbeat Detection and Display Logic

The display uses numerical validity checks to decide whether a measurement should be shown.

### Heart-rate check

```cpp
bool validHR =
    heartRate >= 30.0f &&
    heartRate <= 220.0f;
```

This accepts values between 30 and 220 BPM.

### SpO₂ check

```cpp
bool validSpO2 =
    spo2 >= 70.0f &&
    spo2 <= 100.0f;
```

This accepts values between 70% and 100%.

If a value falls outside the configured range, the display shows a placeholder rather than the numerical value.

**Important limitation:** These checks only reject values outside the selected numerical ranges. They do not prove that a finger is present, that the optical signal is strong enough, or that the reading is accurate.

The current firmware should therefore be considered a prototype. A more robust implementation should use explicit finger-presence detection, signal-quality assessment, and a validated measurement algorithm.

